@jnothman @NicolasHug @amueller 

Hopefully you remember this one. Here are some further enhancements/fixes:
1) includes signed rank-sum hypothesis testing; 
2) the `se` rule is now implemented as standard-error rather than just SD as in the example `plot_grid_search_refit_callable.py`; 
3) more mature error-handling is implemented;
4) boilerplate and business logic has been removed, cognitive complexity reduced;
5) at reviewer's request, what was formerly a single class has now been organized into its own dedicated module;
6) docstring, doctesting, commenting, and comprehensive unit testing is now present (see `test_refit_callable_` in model_selection/tests/test_subselect.py
7) the `plot_grid_search_refit_callable.py` has also now been updated to leverage the newly added `_subselect` tools and explore the statistical advantages to using them w.r.t. mitigating train-test deviance and promoting greater tuning generalizability.
8) documentation for grid_search has been updated to add brief background on the theory and explanation of usage.

## Reference Issues/PRs
https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/blob/master/examples/model_selection/plot_grid_search_refit_callable.py
https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/blob/master/examples/model_selection/plot_grid_search_digits.py
https://scikit-learn.org/stable/auto_examples/model_selection/plot_grid_search_digits.html
See also https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/11269. See also https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/pull/11354. See also https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/12865. See also https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/9499. 

## What does this implement/fix? Explain your changes.
This PR formalizes methods for generating custom refit callables that can be used with `GridSearchCV` and `RandomSearchCV`. This new feature was partly motivated by discussions with other members of the Scikit-Learn team who expressed interest and assisted in developing the initial prototype. Since then, it has seen considerable renewed interest from other users in the scikit-learn and Kaggle communities, many of whom were surprised that the refit callable method for the "One Standard Error Rule" wasn't already implemented in the package. Rather than contribute that functionality specifically, which could arguably be too opinionated, I've attempted to generalize that strategy so that users can exploit `refit` for "model (sub)selection" based on any of a number of strategies.

## Any other comments?
- McNemar’s test, Shapiro-Wilk and others might be nice additions beyond Wilcoxon down the road but I think would go beyond the scope of this PR. Other custom selectors like these might be best left to the user to create, or if there is sufficient community interest, added formally to the core collection in `_subselect.py` through future PR's.

